{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB09113 - MONDO_6502",
  "verbalization": "Poractant Alfa is implicated in the pathogenesis of Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome (ARDS) through a chain of indications that link it to Newborn Respiratory Distress Syndrome (NRDS) and subsequently to ARDS. The evidence suggests that Poractant Alfa, a surfactant replacement therapy, is used in the treatment of NRDS, which is a condition characterized by respiratory failure in newborns. The indirect pathway involves Colfosceril Palmitate and Beractant, both of which are also used in the management of NRDS, and they are indicated for ARDS. This suggests a potential mechanistic link where Poractant Alfa may exert a role in the pathophysiology of ARDS through its effects on respiratory function and inflammation, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The strong scores in the evidence support a plausible relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Poractant Alfa in the development of ARDS.",
